WEBVTT

00:00:06.824 --> 00:00:09.795
The Wonderful Wizard of Oz by L.

00:00:09.855 --> 00:00:11.216
Frank Baum.

00:00:11.276 --> 00:00:24.835
Copyright Black Cat Publishing.

00:00:24.895 --> 00:00:55.908
Chapter 1 The Munchkins Dorothy lives in a small grey house in Kansas with her uncle Henry and M and little dog Toto.

00:00:55.968 --> 00:00:59.052
Everything in Kansas is grey.

00:00:59.112 --> 00:01:03.905
There are no trees or flowers, but there are cyclones.

00:01:03.964 --> 00:01:07.306
Cyclones are very strong winds.

00:01:07.366 --> 00:01:11.139
They can sometimes blow people and houses away.

00:01:11.198 --> 00:01:14.800
One day, Uncle Henry looks at the grey sky.

00:01:14.860 --> 00:01:17.592
He says, A cyclone is coming.

00:01:17.652 --> 00:01:19.403
We must go to the cellar.

00:01:19.463 --> 00:01:21.634
Come with us quickly, Dorothy.

00:01:21.694 --> 00:01:23.075
Says Aunt Em.

00:01:23.135 --> 00:01:27.378
They run to the door of the cellar, but Toto is afraid.

00:01:27.438 --> 00:01:30.469
He runs into the bedroom and under the bed.

00:01:30.529 --> 00:01:32.376
Dorothy runs after him.

00:01:32.436 --> 00:01:35.108
Leave Toto and come to the cellar now!

00:01:35.168 --> 00:01:36.741
Cries at him.

00:01:36.801 --> 00:01:41.029
Dorothy picks Toto up and runs to the door of the cellar.

00:01:41.089 --> 00:01:46.170
But at that moment, something strange happens.

00:01:46.230 --> 00:01:57.340
The cyclone is very strong, and it picks the house up and takes it, with Dorothy and Toto inside, into the sky.

00:01:57.400 --> 00:02:01.403
Uncle Henry and Aunt Em can only watch from the cellar.

00:02:01.463 --> 00:02:06.206
The house flies and flies in the sky for many hours.

00:02:06.266 --> 00:02:09.968
Dorothy and Toto are alone and afraid.

00:02:10.028 --> 00:02:15.482
After some time, they become very tired, and they fall asleep.

00:02:15.541 --> 00:02:21.216
When they wake up, the house is on the ground.

00:02:21.276 --> 00:02:25.260
Everything is quiet.

00:02:25.320 --> 00:02:29.674
Dorothy opens the door quietly and goes out.

00:02:29.734 --> 00:02:36.990
It is a sunny day, and she sees tall trees and beautiful flowers everywhere.

00:02:37.050 --> 00:02:39.342
This isn't Kansas, Toto.

00:02:39.402 --> 00:02:40.472
Says Dorothy.

00:02:40.532 --> 00:02:41.754
Where are we?

00:02:41.814 --> 00:02:43.523
And who are those people?

00:02:43.583 --> 00:02:47.854
Dorothy can see three short men and an old woman.

00:02:47.914 --> 00:02:53.308
The men are wearing blue hats, blue clothes, and blue shoes.

00:02:53.367 --> 00:02:57.260
The old woman is wearing a beautiful white dress.

00:02:57.319 --> 00:03:02.200
She looks at Dorothy and says, We are very happy.

00:03:02.260 --> 00:03:03.941
You bring good luck.

00:03:04.001 --> 00:03:06.812
The Wicked Witch of the East is dead.

00:03:06.872 --> 00:03:08.963
The Munchkins are her people.

00:03:09.023 --> 00:03:11.884
They're happy now because she's dead.

00:03:11.944 --> 00:03:14.314
Thank you, dear girl.

00:03:14.374 --> 00:03:16.275
Dorothy is surprised.

00:03:16.335 --> 00:03:17.576
I don't understand.

00:03:17.636 --> 00:03:18.826
She says.

00:03:18.886 --> 00:03:22.297
The old woman and the Munchkins smile at her.

00:03:22.357 --> 00:03:26.259
Look, the Wicked Witch of the East is under your house.

00:03:26.319 --> 00:03:27.719
Says the old woman.

00:03:27.779 --> 00:03:30.468
Look, you can see her feet.

00:03:30.528 --> 00:03:34.831
Dorothy sees two feet with silver shoes under her house.

00:03:34.891 --> 00:03:37.634
She jumps back in surprise.

00:03:37.694 --> 00:03:44.255
The old woman takes the silver shoes from the wicked witch's feet and gives them to Dorothy.

00:03:44.315 --> 00:03:46.562
They're your shoes now.

00:03:46.622 --> 00:03:51.174
You must wear them because a witch's shoes can do great things.

00:03:51.234 --> 00:03:52.986
But are you a witch too?

00:03:53.046 --> 00:03:54.347
Ask Dorothy.

00:03:54.406 --> 00:03:57.019
Yes, I'm the witch of the North.

00:03:57.078 --> 00:03:58.430
I'm a good witch.

00:03:58.490 --> 00:04:00.001
A good witch?

00:04:00.060 --> 00:04:01.642
I don't understand.

00:04:01.701 --> 00:04:02.842
Where are we?

00:04:02.902 --> 00:04:04.073
Says Dorothy.

00:04:04.133 --> 00:04:06.335
We're in the Land of Oz.

00:04:06.395 --> 00:04:09.507
Here in the Land of Oz, there are four witches.

00:04:09.567 --> 00:04:11.173
Says the witch of the North.

00:04:11.233 --> 00:04:15.411
The witches of the North and South are very good witches.

00:04:15.471 --> 00:04:20.995
But the wicked witches of the East and the West are very bad witches.

00:04:21.055 --> 00:04:24.388
Now the wicked witch of the East is dead.

00:04:24.448 --> 00:04:29.211
There's only one wicked witch, the wicked witch of the West.

00:04:29.271 --> 00:04:32.013
Can you please help me go home to Kansas?

00:04:32.073 --> 00:04:33.244
Ask Dorothy.

00:04:33.304 --> 00:04:34.385
Kansas?

00:04:34.445 --> 00:04:35.946
Where's Kansas?

00:04:36.006 --> 00:04:37.453
Ask the good witch.

00:04:37.512 --> 00:04:40.090
I'm sorry, but I can't help you.

00:04:40.150 --> 00:04:44.554
You must go and see the Wizard of Oz in the Emerald City.

00:04:44.614 --> 00:04:47.567
He's a good wizard, and he can help you.

00:04:47.627 --> 00:04:49.488
Where is the Emerald City?

00:04:49.548 --> 00:04:50.640
Ask Dorothy.

00:04:50.700 --> 00:04:52.311
It is far away.

00:04:52.371 --> 00:04:53.833
You must walk there.

00:04:53.892 --> 00:04:55.244
Says the good witch.

00:04:55.304 --> 00:04:56.776
Can you come with me?

00:04:56.836 --> 00:04:58.168
Ask Dorothy.

00:04:58.228 --> 00:05:02.600
No, I can't come with you, but I can give you my kiss.

00:05:02.660 --> 00:05:04.271
Says the good witch.

00:05:04.331 --> 00:05:07.532
She gives Dorothy a kiss on her forehead.

00:05:07.592 --> 00:05:12.075
Her kiss is special and looks like a little red flower.

00:05:12.135 --> 00:05:14.246
No, nothing can hurt you.

00:05:14.306 --> 00:05:15.667
Says the good witch.

00:05:15.727 --> 00:05:19.368
The yellow brick road goes to the Emerald City.

00:05:19.428 --> 00:05:21.710
Follow the yellow brick road.

00:05:21.770 --> 00:05:23.972
Goodbye, my dear.

00:05:24.032 --> 00:05:25.343
Goodbye.

00:05:25.403 --> 00:05:26.724
Says Dorothy.

00:05:26.784 --> 00:05:30.728
She goes to her house and puts some bread in the basket.

00:05:30.787 --> 00:05:35.492
Then she puts on a clean dress and the wicked witch's silver shoes.

00:05:35.552 --> 00:05:37.844
Let's go to the Emerald City, Toto.

00:05:37.904 --> 00:05:41.427
She says.

00:05:41.486 --> 00:05:46.214
Listening activity.

00:05:46.274 --> 00:05:50.350
Hello, my name is Scarecrow.

00:05:50.410 --> 00:05:56.142
I live in the land of the Munchkins and I want to be your friend.

00:05:56.202 --> 00:06:03.746
I don't really like my job because I am very friendly and I don't like scaring the birds.

00:06:03.806 --> 00:06:08.167
I can't change jobs because I am not very clever.

00:06:08.227 --> 00:06:11.489
You see, I don't have a brain.

00:06:11.548 --> 00:06:21.808
I am going to the Emerald City to ask the Wizard of Oz for his help.

00:06:21.867 --> 00:06:41.200
Chapter 2 The Scarecrow It is a sunny day in the land of the munchkins.

00:06:41.260 --> 00:06:46.324
Dorothy and Toto walk along the yellow brick road all day.

00:06:46.384 --> 00:06:51.810
When Dorothy is tired, she sits down by the road near a scarecrow.

00:06:51.869 --> 00:06:55.193
Suddenly, the scarecrow smiles at her.

00:06:55.253 --> 00:06:57.025
She is very surprised.

00:06:57.085 --> 00:06:59.157
Can a scarecrow smile?

00:06:59.217 --> 00:07:00.451
She thinks.

00:07:00.510 --> 00:07:03.434
Then the scarecrow says, Hello!

00:07:03.494 --> 00:07:04.014
Oh!

00:07:04.074 --> 00:07:05.105
says Dorothy.

00:07:05.165 --> 00:07:06.366
You can speak!

00:07:06.426 --> 00:07:07.916
Of course I can speak!

00:07:07.976 --> 00:07:09.417
Says the scarecrow.

00:07:09.477 --> 00:07:11.258
But I can't move!

00:07:11.318 --> 00:07:12.898
Can you help me?

00:07:12.958 --> 00:07:16.560
Dorothy helps the scarecrow to move from his post.

00:07:16.620 --> 00:07:18.541
Thank you very much!

00:07:18.601 --> 00:07:21.632
He says, moving his arms and legs.

00:07:21.692 --> 00:07:24.668
They're straw everywhere.

00:07:24.728 --> 00:07:25.973
Who are you?

00:07:26.033 --> 00:07:26.944
He asks.

00:07:27.004 --> 00:07:28.595
And where are you going?

00:07:28.655 --> 00:07:30.316
My name is Dorothy.

00:07:30.376 --> 00:07:32.348
I'm going to the Emerald City.

00:07:32.408 --> 00:07:34.580
I must find the Wizard of Oz.

00:07:34.640 --> 00:07:37.082
He can help me go back home to Kansas.

00:07:37.142 --> 00:07:39.244
Where is the Emerald City?

00:07:39.304 --> 00:07:42.206
He asks, and who is the Wizard of Oz?

00:07:42.266 --> 00:07:43.327
Don't you know?

00:07:43.387 --> 00:07:44.508
Ask Dorothy.

00:07:44.568 --> 00:07:45.129
No.

00:07:45.149 --> 00:07:47.320
I don't know anything.

00:07:47.380 --> 00:07:50.674
He says, I don't have a brain in my head.

00:07:50.734 --> 00:07:52.600
I only have straw.

00:07:52.660 --> 00:07:55.365
I'm very sorry, says Dorothy.

00:07:55.425 --> 00:07:58.336
I want a brain, says the Scarecrow.

00:07:58.396 --> 00:08:01.127
Can the Wizard of Oz give me a brain?

00:08:01.187 --> 00:08:02.937
I don't know, says Dorothy.

00:08:02.997 --> 00:08:05.048
But you can come with me and ask him.

00:08:05.108 --> 00:08:07.899
Thank you, says the Scarecrow.

00:08:07.959 --> 00:08:11.331
Toto looks at the Scarecrow and starts barking.

00:08:11.391 --> 00:08:13.073
Don't be afraid of Toto.

00:08:13.133 --> 00:08:14.294
He's a good dog.

00:08:14.354 --> 00:08:15.424
Says Dorothy.

00:08:15.484 --> 00:08:18.036
Oh, I'm not afraid of anything.

00:08:18.096 --> 00:08:20.798
Well, I am afraid of fire.

00:08:20.857 --> 00:08:22.238
Says the Scarecrow.

00:08:22.298 --> 00:08:24.110
Let me carry your basket.

00:08:24.170 --> 00:08:26.180
I never get tired.

00:08:26.240 --> 00:08:30.864
Dorothy Toto and the Scarecrow walk along the yellow brick road.

00:08:30.924 --> 00:08:36.636
Soon Dorothy is hungry, so she and Toto eat some bread from the basket.

00:08:36.696 --> 00:08:38.667
Do you want some bread, Scarecrow?

00:08:38.727 --> 00:08:39.788
Ask Dorothy.

00:08:39.848 --> 00:08:41.549
No, thank you, he says.

00:08:41.609 --> 00:08:43.240
I'm never hungry.

00:08:43.300 --> 00:08:45.642
Please tell me about your home.

00:08:45.702 --> 00:08:48.354
Kansas is a dry, grey place.

00:08:48.414 --> 00:08:51.486
There are no trees and no flowers.

00:08:51.546 --> 00:08:54.108
There are cyclones every year.

00:08:54.168 --> 00:08:57.960
I live in a little house with my aunt, Em, and Uncle Henry.

00:08:58.020 --> 00:09:01.283
Why do you want to go back to Grey, Kansas?"

00:09:01.343 --> 00:09:02.894
asks the Scarecrow.

00:09:02.954 --> 00:09:05.656
This country is very beautiful.

00:09:05.716 --> 00:09:08.598
There are a lot of trees and flowers.

00:09:08.658 --> 00:09:10.189
I don't understand.

00:09:10.249 --> 00:09:13.501
You don't understand, because you don't have a brain.

00:09:13.561 --> 00:09:14.742
Says Dorothy.

00:09:14.802 --> 00:09:18.474
Kansas is my home, and I love my home.

00:09:18.534 --> 00:09:20.776
My aunt and uncle live there.

00:09:20.836 --> 00:09:23.718
The Scarecrow looks at her and smiles.

00:09:23.778 --> 00:09:26.290
Dorothy and Toto finish their bread.

00:09:26.350 --> 00:09:27.671
Well, let's go.

00:09:27.730 --> 00:09:28.701
Says Dorothy.

00:09:28.761 --> 00:09:31.362
The Emerald City is far away.

00:09:31.422 --> 00:09:34.483
In the evening, Dorothy is tired.

00:09:34.543 --> 00:09:37.624
They see a little house behind some trees.

00:09:37.684 --> 00:09:40.956
No one is in the house, so they go in.

00:09:41.016 --> 00:09:43.387
Dorothy and Toto sleep.

00:09:43.447 --> 00:09:45.408
But the Scarecrow doesn't.

00:09:45.468 --> 00:09:47.728
He laughs and says...

00:09:47.788 --> 00:09:52.530
Scarecrows don't sleep?

00:09:52.590 --> 00:09:56.911
Listening activity.

00:09:56.971 --> 00:10:00.414
So Scarecrow, is your job very boring?

00:10:00.474 --> 00:10:02.366
It's not boring at all.

00:10:02.426 --> 00:10:05.712
In fact, I do a lot of different things.

00:10:05.772 --> 00:10:07.644
Can you keep a secret?

00:10:07.704 --> 00:10:09.577
Yes, of course.

00:10:09.637 --> 00:10:11.489
So what do you do all day?

00:10:11.549 --> 00:10:18.780
Well, when the farmer leaves in the morning, I always wait for five minutes before I get off my post.

00:10:18.840 --> 00:10:26.893
I like reading about what is happening in the news, so I often read the farmer's newspaper, the Munchkin Times.

00:10:26.953 --> 00:10:31.615
After I finish the newspaper, I sometimes practice the violin.

00:10:31.635 --> 00:10:35.286
I am learning to play and I love it.

00:10:35.346 --> 00:10:38.167
It's such a beautiful musical instrument.

00:10:38.227 --> 00:10:43.458
Then in the afternoons, I usually go to see some of my friends in the area.

00:10:43.518 --> 00:10:46.269
There are lots of scarecrows here, you know.

00:10:46.329 --> 00:10:47.859
How do you travel around?

00:10:47.919 --> 00:10:49.090
Do you drive?

00:10:49.150 --> 00:10:50.130
Oh, no.

00:10:50.190 --> 00:10:51.781
I never drive.

00:10:51.840 --> 00:10:55.512
The farmer has a big tractor, but I don't like it.

00:10:55.572 --> 00:10:59.162
It's too noisy, and there's always a lot of smoke.

00:10:59.222 --> 00:11:01.373
I usually ride my bicycle.

00:11:01.432 --> 00:11:03.784
What do you and your friends usually do?

00:11:03.844 --> 00:11:08.470
Some of my friends like sports, so they often play tennis.

00:11:08.530 --> 00:11:13.055
I hardly ever play because I don't really like tennis.

00:11:13.114 --> 00:11:17.270
I usually play some card games with three or four friends.

00:11:17.329 --> 00:11:19.641
We can talk at the same time.

00:11:19.701 --> 00:11:22.120
What about when it is very hot and sunny?

00:11:22.180 --> 00:11:23.331
Do you sunbathe?

00:11:23.391 --> 00:11:29.382
But Dorothy, I never sunbathe because it is very dangerous for scarecrows.

00:11:29.442 --> 00:11:36.824
I'm very afraid of it because I don't want to catch fire.

00:11:36.884 --> 00:11:41.741
Cyclones.

00:11:41.801 --> 00:11:46.368
Sometimes very big storms become cyclones.

00:11:46.428 --> 00:11:51.650
Strong winds blow in opposite directions and make a shape like a funnel.

00:11:51.710 --> 00:12:00.676
When this powerful funnel touches the earth, it can blow everything away, people, animals, and even cars and houses.

00:12:00.736 --> 00:12:09.137
In the United States, there are approximately 1,000 reports of cyclones every year, but not all of these are dangerous.

00:12:09.197 --> 00:12:13.070
In fact, only about 10 to 20 are violent.

00:12:13.130 --> 00:12:21.836
Cyclones are very common in some of the central states, such as Texas, Oklahoma, Kansas, and Colorado.

00:12:21.896 --> 00:12:27.357
They usually happen between April and October because of the warm temperatures.

00:12:27.417 --> 00:12:40.041
On average, a cyclone lasts for about 15 to 20 minutes and can move from 75 miles, 131 kilometers to 300 miles, 480 kilometers per hour.

00:12:40.101 --> 00:12:47.594
Some people are very interested in cyclones and like to follow them in their cars.

00:12:47.654 --> 00:12:52.335
Some are scientists, but some other people do this as a hobby.

00:12:52.395 --> 00:12:56.726
They write about each cyclone, take photos and make films.

00:12:56.786 --> 00:13:07.329
It is very dangerous, but it can help us understand more about what cyclones can do and why they happen.

00:13:07.389 --> 00:13:16.036
Listening activity Hello, I'm the Tin Woodman.

00:13:16.096 --> 00:13:19.688
I live in a little house in the forest.

00:13:19.748 --> 00:13:26.832
I have a tin body and I carry an axe because I cut down trees.

00:13:26.892 --> 00:13:33.795
I have an oil can too because I must put oil on my arms and legs.

00:13:33.855 --> 00:13:39.685
I'm sad because I don't love anyone.

00:13:39.745 --> 00:13:44.084
Hello, I'm the lion.

00:13:44.104 --> 00:13:48.275
I live in the forest with other animals.

00:13:48.335 --> 00:13:52.046
I'm scary because I'm big.

00:13:52.106 --> 00:13:57.608
I have a big mouth, big teeth, and a long tail.

00:13:57.668 --> 00:14:03.249
I am very strong and can carry people on my back.

00:14:03.309 --> 00:14:15.410
I make a lot of noise, but I don't bite anyone because I'm afraid.

00:14:15.470 --> 00:14:37.550
Chapter 3 The Tin Woodman and the Lion The next morning, Dorothy and the Scarecrow hear a loud noise outside the house.

00:14:37.610 --> 00:14:38.768
What's that?

00:14:38.828 --> 00:14:40.140
Ask Dorothy.

00:14:40.200 --> 00:14:41.522
I don't know.

00:14:41.582 --> 00:14:43.033
Says the Scarecrow.

00:14:43.093 --> 00:14:44.575
Let's go and see.

00:14:44.635 --> 00:14:47.518
They run out of the house to the trees.

00:14:47.578 --> 00:14:50.972
They see a strange tin man by a tree.

00:14:51.032 --> 00:14:53.144
He has an axe in his hands.

00:14:53.204 --> 00:14:54.236
Help!

00:14:54.296 --> 00:14:55.317
Help!

00:14:55.377 --> 00:14:57.106
Cries the strange man.

00:14:57.166 --> 00:14:58.413
What's the matter?

00:14:58.473 --> 00:14:59.654
Ask Dorothy.

00:14:59.714 --> 00:15:01.395
I can't move.

00:15:01.455 --> 00:15:02.686
Says the tin woodman.

00:15:02.746 --> 00:15:06.780
Can you put some oil on my arms and legs, please?

00:15:06.840 --> 00:15:09.392
There's an oil can in my house.

00:15:09.452 --> 00:15:13.394
Dorothy runs back to the house and gets the oil can.

00:15:13.454 --> 00:15:18.799
She takes it to the tin woodman and they put some oil on his arms and legs.

00:15:18.859 --> 00:15:21.451
He slowly begins to move.

00:15:21.511 --> 00:15:23.802
First, he moves his head.

00:15:23.863 --> 00:15:26.626
Then his arms and legs.

00:15:26.686 --> 00:15:27.907
Thank you.

00:15:27.967 --> 00:15:30.781
He says, I feel better now.

00:15:30.840 --> 00:15:34.324
Sometimes I get wet in the rain.

00:15:34.384 --> 00:15:38.519
Water is very bad for my tin body.

00:15:38.579 --> 00:15:40.249
Who are you?

00:15:40.309 --> 00:15:42.309
And where are you going?

00:15:42.369 --> 00:15:45.170
I'm Dorothy and this is the Scarecrow.

00:15:45.230 --> 00:15:51.443
We're going to the Emerald City to find the Wizard of Oz because he can help me go back to Kansas.

00:15:51.503 --> 00:15:54.264
Perhaps he can also give the Scarecrow a brain.

00:15:54.324 --> 00:15:57.776
Can the Wizard of Oz give me a heart?

00:15:57.836 --> 00:15:59.367
Asks the Tin Woodman.

00:15:59.427 --> 00:16:04.489
I don't have a heart and I can't love anyone.

00:16:04.549 --> 00:16:07.280
There is no happiness without love.

00:16:07.340 --> 00:16:09.041
Why don't you come with us?

00:16:09.101 --> 00:16:10.392
Says the Scarecrow.

00:16:10.452 --> 00:16:13.203
Yes, you can ask the wizard for a heart.

00:16:13.263 --> 00:16:14.303
Says Dorothy.

00:16:14.363 --> 00:16:16.253
Thank you, my friends.

00:16:16.313 --> 00:16:17.914
Says the Tin Woodman.

00:16:17.974 --> 00:16:20.174
And they start walking again.

00:16:20.234 --> 00:16:24.395
The three friends in Toto walk along the yellow brick road.

00:16:24.455 --> 00:16:27.676
They look at all the tall trees near the road.

00:16:27.736 --> 00:16:32.697
There are a lot of noises coming from the different animals behind the trees.

00:16:32.757 --> 00:16:36.308
Suddenly, a lion jumps out into the road.

00:16:36.368 --> 00:16:42.602
He opens his big mouth and roars.

00:16:42.662 --> 00:16:48.926
He has big teeth and wants to bite Toto.

00:16:48.986 --> 00:16:55.162
Dorothy is afraid for Toto and she runs to the lion and hits him on the nose with her basket.

00:16:55.222 --> 00:16:56.543
Don't hurt my dog.

00:16:56.603 --> 00:16:58.044
She cries angrily.

00:16:58.104 --> 00:16:59.876
He's small and you're big.

00:16:59.896 --> 00:17:02.568
Don't hit me please.

00:17:02.628 --> 00:17:03.900
Says the lion.

00:17:03.959 --> 00:17:05.561
You're afraid.

00:17:05.621 --> 00:17:06.604
Says Dorothy.

00:17:06.665 --> 00:17:09.288
You're a lion and you're afraid.

00:17:09.348 --> 00:17:10.699
You're a coward.

00:17:10.759 --> 00:17:12.910
Yes, I am a coward.

00:17:12.970 --> 00:17:16.842
Lions must be courageous, but I'm not.

00:17:16.903 --> 00:17:20.224
I make a lot of noise, but I am a coward.

00:17:20.284 --> 00:17:24.827
Says the lion sadly as he starts crying.

00:17:24.887 --> 00:17:27.328
Don't cry.

00:17:27.388 --> 00:17:28.439
Says Dorothy.

00:17:28.499 --> 00:17:30.740
Come with us to the Emerald City.

00:17:30.800 --> 00:17:34.404
Perhaps the Wizard of Oz can give you courage.

00:17:34.464 --> 00:17:38.990
So they all continue walking along the yellow brick road.

00:17:39.050 --> 00:17:41.912
At one point, they see a big river.

00:17:41.972 --> 00:17:43.684
How can we cross the river?

00:17:43.744 --> 00:17:45.124
Ask Dorothy.

00:17:45.184 --> 00:17:49.555
The lion looks at the river and says, I can jump across.

00:17:49.615 --> 00:17:51.624
But I'm afraid.

00:17:51.684 --> 00:17:54.386
Don't be afraid, says the Scarecrow.

00:17:54.446 --> 00:17:56.408
You're a strong lion.

00:17:56.468 --> 00:17:59.460
You can take us on your back one by one.

00:17:59.480 --> 00:18:01.231
Oh, all right.

00:18:01.292 --> 00:18:02.532
I can do that.

00:18:02.592 --> 00:18:03.643
Says the lion.

00:18:03.703 --> 00:18:09.028
You don't have a brain, but you have good ideas, Scarecrow.

00:18:09.088 --> 00:18:12.110
And so the lion jumps across the river.

00:18:12.170 --> 00:18:17.830
He takes the Scarecrow first, and then he takes Dorothy and Toto.

00:18:17.890 --> 00:18:23.130
He takes the Tin Woodman last.

00:18:23.190 --> 00:18:30.684
Listening activity Where do lions live?

00:18:30.744 --> 00:18:34.256
Most lions today live in parts of Africa.

00:18:34.316 --> 00:18:37.668
Lions like areas with lots of grass.

00:18:37.728 --> 00:18:40.519
How many lions are there in the world?

00:18:40.579 --> 00:18:44.298
Today there are about 20,000 lions in Africa.

00:18:44.358 --> 00:18:46.716
How long do they live?

00:18:46.776 --> 00:18:51.018
In captivity, lions can live for about 25 years.

00:18:51.078 --> 00:18:55.900
In the wild, they usually only live for about 8 to 10 years.

00:18:55.961 --> 00:18:57.791
How do they live?

00:18:57.851 --> 00:19:02.554
Lions are social animals, and they live in groups called a pride.

00:19:02.614 --> 00:19:06.726
Some prides are very small, and some are very big.

00:19:06.786 --> 00:19:09.629
Most have about 15 lions.

00:19:09.689 --> 00:19:14.093
What differences are there between males and females?

00:19:14.153 --> 00:19:18.756
Male lions have long hair around their face called a mane.

00:19:18.816 --> 00:19:23.406
Male lions protect the pride when the female lions look for food.

00:19:23.466 --> 00:19:25.332
How big are they?

00:19:25.392 --> 00:19:32.784
An adult male can be about 2 meters long and can weigh from 170 to 230 kilograms.

00:19:32.844 --> 00:19:41.504
An adult female is smaller at about 1.5 meters long and with a weight of about 120 to 180 kilograms.

00:19:41.564 --> 00:19:45.333
How often do they have cubs?

00:19:45.393 --> 00:19:53.628
Lions in captivity can have cubs every year, but lions in the wild usually have cubs only every two years.

00:19:53.688 --> 00:20:02.943
The lioness can have from one to six cubs at a time.

00:20:03.003 --> 00:20:20.847
Chapter 4 The Emerald City The four friends walk all day.

00:20:20.907 --> 00:20:26.580
In the evening they see some little green houses and some little people in green clothes.

00:20:26.640 --> 00:20:29.242
Everything's green, says Dorothy.

00:20:29.302 --> 00:20:31.322
We are near the Emerald City.

00:20:31.382 --> 00:20:34.474
Soon they come to a big green door.

00:20:34.534 --> 00:20:41.768
It opens slowly and they see a little man in green clothes and green glasses.

00:20:41.828 --> 00:20:45.618
We want to see the Wizard of Oz, please," says Dorothy.

00:20:45.678 --> 00:20:48.789
Okay, follow me, says the little man.

00:20:48.849 --> 00:20:51.110
But first, put these on.

00:20:51.170 --> 00:20:57.601
He opens a big box, and inside there are lots of pears of green glasses.

00:20:57.661 --> 00:21:00.012
You must wear these glasses.

00:21:00.072 --> 00:21:03.233
Everybody in the Emerald City wears them.

00:21:03.293 --> 00:21:07.464
So they put on the glasses and go into the Emerald City.

00:21:07.524 --> 00:21:10.972
They stop in front of the Palace of Oz.

00:21:11.032 --> 00:21:13.256
A man opens the door.

00:21:13.316 --> 00:21:15.532
Follow me, he says.

00:21:15.592 --> 00:21:19.056
He takes them into a big green room.

00:21:19.116 --> 00:21:21.824
Now, wait here until I call you.

00:21:21.884 --> 00:21:26.888
When he returns, he says, the wizard wants to see the girl first.

00:21:26.948 --> 00:21:30.050
Dorothy goes into a beautiful room.

00:21:30.110 --> 00:21:37.146
On a green chair, there is only a very big head, without a body, arms or legs.

00:21:37.206 --> 00:21:40.238
She is surprised and afraid.

00:21:40.298 --> 00:21:42.270
I am Oz.

00:21:42.330 --> 00:21:43.681
Says the big head.

00:21:43.741 --> 00:21:46.410
Who are you and what do you want?

00:21:46.471 --> 00:21:49.950
I'm Dorothy, and I want to go home to Kansas.

00:21:50.010 --> 00:21:51.452
I don't know the way.

00:21:51.512 --> 00:21:53.534
Can you help me, please?

00:21:53.594 --> 00:21:56.896
The big eyes open and close.

00:21:56.956 --> 00:21:59.798
Then the mouth opens and speaks.

00:21:59.858 --> 00:22:01.810
Perhaps I can help you.

00:22:01.870 --> 00:22:06.293
But first, you must kill the wicked witch of the West.

00:22:06.353 --> 00:22:07.404
Oh, no.

00:22:07.464 --> 00:22:08.584
Says Dorothy.

00:22:08.644 --> 00:22:10.584
I don't want to kill anyone.

00:22:10.644 --> 00:22:13.574
The Wicked Witch of the East is dead.

00:22:13.634 --> 00:22:16.526
You're wearing her silver shoes.

00:22:16.546 --> 00:22:21.571
Now, go and kill the Wicked Witch of the West.

00:22:21.631 --> 00:22:24.884
How can I kill the Wicked Witch of the West?

00:22:24.944 --> 00:22:25.925
She asks.

00:22:25.985 --> 00:22:27.314
Where is she?

00:22:27.374 --> 00:22:30.264
The head does not answer.

00:22:30.324 --> 00:22:34.454
Dorothy leaves the room, and the scarecrow goes in.

00:22:34.514 --> 00:22:37.475
But the scarecrow does not see a big head.

00:22:37.535 --> 00:22:40.606
He sees a beautiful woman.

00:22:40.666 --> 00:22:42.386
Oh, great Oz.

00:22:42.446 --> 00:22:46.357
Please give me a brain, says the scarecrow.

00:22:46.417 --> 00:22:51.388
First, you must kill the wicked witch of the West.

00:22:51.448 --> 00:22:53.104
Says Oz.

00:22:53.164 --> 00:22:56.202
The Tin Woodman enters the green room.

00:22:56.262 --> 00:23:03.588
He sees an ugly monster with five eyes, five arms, and five legs.

00:23:03.648 --> 00:23:06.742
Oh, great Oz, please give me a heart.

00:23:06.802 --> 00:23:08.242
Says the Tin Woodman.

00:23:08.302 --> 00:23:13.928
First, you must help Dorothy and the Scarecrow kill the Wicked Witch of the West.

00:23:13.988 --> 00:23:15.273
Says Oz.

00:23:15.333 --> 00:23:20.200
The tin woodman leaves the room, and the lion goes in.

00:23:20.260 --> 00:23:23.431
He sees a big ball of fire.

00:23:23.491 --> 00:23:24.892
He is afraid.

00:23:24.952 --> 00:23:28.754
Oh, great Oz, please give me courage.

00:23:28.814 --> 00:23:30.114
Says the lion.

00:23:30.174 --> 00:23:36.327
I can only give you courage when the Wicked Witch of the West is dead.

00:23:36.387 --> 00:23:40.841
When the friends meet, they talk about the strange wizard.

00:23:40.901 --> 00:23:44.438
Now we must find the wicked witch of the West and kill her.

00:23:44.498 --> 00:23:45.490
Says Dorothy.

00:23:45.550 --> 00:23:46.983
Yes, we must.

00:23:47.043 --> 00:23:48.738
They all say.

00:23:48.798 --> 00:23:53.863
The friends leave the Emerald City to find the Wicked Witch of the West.

00:23:53.923 --> 00:23:58.814
On their way out, they give their glasses to the little man at the gate.

00:23:58.875 --> 00:24:02.636
Dorothy asks him, Where is the Wicked Witch of the West?

00:24:02.696 --> 00:24:04.016
We must find her.

00:24:04.076 --> 00:24:06.877
She lives in the Land of the Wing Keys.

00:24:06.937 --> 00:24:09.648
He says, You must walk to the West.

00:24:09.708 --> 00:24:11.008
Be careful.

00:24:11.068 --> 00:24:15.560
She is very bad and everyone is afraid of her.

00:24:15.620 --> 00:24:23.098
So Dorothy, the Scarecrow, the Tin Woodman, the Lion and Toto start walking to the West.

00:24:23.158 --> 00:24:26.020
They walk for a long time.

00:24:26.080 --> 00:24:31.785
Above them in her castle, the Wicked Witch of the West watches them.

00:24:31.845 --> 00:24:36.379
The Wicked Witch has a magic eye and can see everything.

00:24:36.439 --> 00:24:38.991
Who are those people on my road?

00:24:39.052 --> 00:24:46.335
She says angrily.

00:24:46.395 --> 00:25:09.270
Chapter 5 The Wicked Witch of the West The witch blows her silver whistle.

00:25:09.330 --> 00:25:12.654
And forty winged monkeys quickly arrive.

00:25:12.714 --> 00:25:13.864
What do you want?

00:25:13.924 --> 00:25:16.085
The king of the winged monkeys asks.

00:25:16.145 --> 00:25:20.227
There are three people, a dog and a lion on my road.

00:25:20.287 --> 00:25:23.978
She says, go and kill the people and the dog.

00:25:24.038 --> 00:25:25.879
But bring me the lion.

00:25:25.939 --> 00:25:28.430
He is big and strong.

00:25:28.490 --> 00:25:29.890
He can work for me.

00:25:29.950 --> 00:25:31.741
Yes, immediately.

00:25:31.801 --> 00:25:35.517
Say the winged monkeys and they fly away.

00:25:35.577 --> 00:25:40.314
They quickly reach the road and see the four friends and the dog.

00:25:40.374 --> 00:25:43.434
They break the tin woodman's arms and legs.

00:25:43.494 --> 00:25:48.166
They take the straw out of the scarecrow and throw his clothes into a tree.

00:25:48.226 --> 00:25:51.718
Then they take the lion to the wicked witch's castle.

00:25:51.778 --> 00:25:59.260
The winged monkeys do not hurt Dorothy in total because they see the good witch's kiss on Dorothy's forehead.

00:25:59.320 --> 00:26:04.092
They decide to take them to the wicked witch's castle with the lion.

00:26:04.152 --> 00:26:09.294
The wicked witch sees the kiss on Dorothy's face and she is afraid.

00:26:09.354 --> 00:26:11.814
But she doesn't say anything.

00:26:11.834 --> 00:26:12.975
Ha ha!

00:26:13.035 --> 00:26:15.085
Now you are my prisoner.

00:26:15.145 --> 00:26:18.166
You must work in my house every day.

00:26:18.226 --> 00:26:20.477
Clean this dirty kitchen.

00:26:20.537 --> 00:26:21.857
She says to Dorothy.

00:26:21.917 --> 00:26:26.289
Remember, I can watch you all the time.

00:26:26.349 --> 00:26:30.486
Dorothy looks at her sadly and starts to clean the kitchen.

00:26:30.546 --> 00:26:33.224
How can I go back to Kansas now?

00:26:33.284 --> 00:26:34.394
She thinks.

00:26:34.454 --> 00:26:36.886
She is very unhappy.

00:26:36.946 --> 00:26:44.432
Dorothy does not know her shoes are magic, but the Wicked Witch knows, and she wants them.

00:26:44.492 --> 00:26:48.005
One morning Dorothy's left shoe falls off.

00:26:48.065 --> 00:26:53.089
The Wicked Witch quickly takes it and says, This is my shoe now.

00:26:53.149 --> 00:26:54.220
No it isn't.

00:26:54.280 --> 00:26:55.901
Christ Dorothy, angrily.

00:26:55.961 --> 00:26:57.039
Give it to me.

00:26:57.100 --> 00:27:01.209
The Wicked Witch then tries to take the other shoe too.

00:27:01.269 --> 00:27:05.542
Dorothy is very angry because she loves her silver shoes.

00:27:05.602 --> 00:27:08.493
She sees a bucket of water near the door.

00:27:08.553 --> 00:27:11.965
She takes it and throws the water at the Wicked Witch.

00:27:12.025 --> 00:27:12.966
No!

00:27:13.026 --> 00:27:14.597
Don't do that!

00:27:14.657 --> 00:27:16.758
Cries the Wicked Witch of the West.

00:27:16.818 --> 00:27:19.230
What a kill me!

00:27:19.290 --> 00:27:20.730
Help!

00:27:20.790 --> 00:27:23.777
Help me please!

00:27:23.837 --> 00:27:33.036
Now on the floor, there is only the wicked witch's black hat, her black dress, and her silver whistle.

00:27:33.096 --> 00:27:36.998
Dorothy looks for her, but cannot find her.

00:27:37.058 --> 00:27:39.589
She puts her left shoe on again.

00:27:39.649 --> 00:27:42.740
Now I am free, and I can help my friends.

00:27:42.800 --> 00:27:46.492
Dorothy says, perhaps I can call the winged monkeys.

00:27:46.552 --> 00:27:50.003
She picks up the witch's silver whistle and looks at it.

00:27:50.063 --> 00:27:51.654
Is this a magic whistle?

00:27:51.714 --> 00:27:52.744
She thinks.

00:27:52.804 --> 00:27:54.804
She blows it.

00:27:54.864 --> 00:27:57.642
and the winged monkeys arrive.

00:27:57.702 --> 00:28:00.003
She is surprised and happy.

00:28:00.063 --> 00:28:02.483
Can you help my friends?

00:28:02.543 --> 00:28:03.434
She asks.

00:28:03.494 --> 00:28:04.284
Yes.

00:28:04.344 --> 00:28:05.584
Says one monkey.

00:28:05.644 --> 00:28:14.546
We always help the person with the magic whistle.

00:28:14.606 --> 00:28:33.908
Chapter 6 Back to the Emerald City The winged monkeys find a lion and free him.

00:28:33.968 --> 00:28:35.740
He is happy now.

00:28:35.800 --> 00:28:40.024
They find the scarecrow's clothes and put some straw in them.

00:28:40.084 --> 00:28:44.588
The scarecrow laughs and says, Thank you.

00:28:44.648 --> 00:28:47.481
Then the winged monkeys help the tin woodman.

00:28:47.541 --> 00:28:50.044
They give him a new oil can.

00:28:50.104 --> 00:28:52.706
Now I can move my arms and legs.

00:28:52.766 --> 00:28:53.697
Thank you.

00:28:53.757 --> 00:28:54.488
He says.

00:28:54.548 --> 00:28:56.800
The Wicked Witch of the West is dead.

00:28:56.860 --> 00:28:58.942
Says Dorothy to her friends.

00:28:59.002 --> 00:29:01.174
Everyone is very happy.

00:29:01.234 --> 00:29:04.287
We must go back to the Wizard of Oz and tell him.

00:29:04.347 --> 00:29:05.328
Says Dorothy.

00:29:05.388 --> 00:29:08.070
The winged monkeys can take us back to the Emerald City.

00:29:08.130 --> 00:29:09.572
Blow the magic whistle.

00:29:09.632 --> 00:29:11.233
Says the Tin Woodman.

00:29:11.293 --> 00:29:13.952
Dorothy blows the whistle.

00:29:14.012 --> 00:29:16.471
And the monkeys come again.

00:29:16.531 --> 00:29:20.203
They carry Dorothy and her friends up into the sky.

00:29:20.263 --> 00:29:23.815
Soon they are at the green door of the Emerald City.

00:29:23.875 --> 00:29:26.806
The little green man opens the door.

00:29:26.866 --> 00:29:30.858
He gives them glasses and takes them to the palace.

00:29:30.918 --> 00:29:35.681
They go to the wizard's room, but no one is there.

00:29:35.741 --> 00:29:39.716
A voice says, I am the Wizard of Oz.

00:29:39.777 --> 00:29:41.131
Where are you?

00:29:41.191 --> 00:29:42.191
Ask Dorothy.

00:29:42.211 --> 00:29:46.054
I am everywhere, but you can't see me.

00:29:46.114 --> 00:29:47.184
Says the wizard.

00:29:47.244 --> 00:29:48.165
Who are you?

00:29:48.225 --> 00:29:49.426
And what do you want?

00:29:49.486 --> 00:29:51.297
Don't you remember us?

00:29:51.357 --> 00:29:52.718
I'm Dorothy.

00:29:52.778 --> 00:29:57.231
I'm here with my friends, the Scarecrow, the Tin Woodman, and the Lion.

00:29:57.291 --> 00:30:01.794
The Wicked Witch of the West is dead, and you must keep your promise.

00:30:01.854 --> 00:30:03.925
I want to go home to Kansas.

00:30:03.985 --> 00:30:06.086
Yes, says the scarecrow.

00:30:06.146 --> 00:30:09.927
The wicked witch is dead, so you must give me a brain.

00:30:09.987 --> 00:30:13.489
And you must give me a heart, says the tinwoodman.

00:30:13.549 --> 00:30:17.015
And I want some courage, says the lion.

00:30:17.075 --> 00:30:20.812
Is the Wicked Witch of the West really dead?"

00:30:20.872 --> 00:30:22.122
asks the wizard.

00:30:22.182 --> 00:30:23.673
Yes, she is.

00:30:23.733 --> 00:30:26.725
They all say, Come back tomorrow.

00:30:26.785 --> 00:30:28.155
Says the wizard.

00:30:28.216 --> 00:30:30.677
I must think about this.

00:30:30.737 --> 00:30:34.318
No, I don't want to come back tomorrow.

00:30:34.378 --> 00:30:35.649
Says the tin woodman.

00:30:35.709 --> 00:30:37.590
I want a heart now.

00:30:37.650 --> 00:30:39.741
And I want a brain now.

00:30:39.801 --> 00:30:41.202
Says the scarecrow.

00:30:41.262 --> 00:30:44.444
I'm angry and I'm going to eat you!"

00:30:44.504 --> 00:30:45.746
says the lion.

00:30:45.806 --> 00:30:49.658
He opens his big mouth and roars.

00:30:49.719 --> 00:30:54.632
Toto, afraid of the lion, jumps up and hits a big screen.

00:30:54.692 --> 00:30:58.305
It falls over.

00:30:58.365 --> 00:31:05.457
And the friends see a little old man with no hair.

00:31:05.517 --> 00:31:07.846
They are very surprised.

00:31:07.906 --> 00:31:11.098
The Tin Woodman is angry and picks up his axe.

00:31:11.158 --> 00:31:12.230
Who are you?

00:31:12.290 --> 00:31:13.902
Asks the Tin Woodman.

00:31:13.962 --> 00:31:16.324
I am Oz.

00:31:16.384 --> 00:31:17.664
Look great.

00:31:17.724 --> 00:31:20.115
Says the little man in a quiet voice.

00:31:20.175 --> 00:31:21.906
Oh, please don't hurt me.

00:31:21.966 --> 00:31:24.908
But the wizard is a big head with no body.

00:31:24.968 --> 00:31:25.949
Says Dorothy.

00:31:26.009 --> 00:31:26.839
No.

00:31:26.899 --> 00:31:28.640
It's a beautiful woman.

00:31:28.700 --> 00:31:29.981
Says the scarecrow.

00:31:30.041 --> 00:31:31.042
You're wrong.

00:31:31.102 --> 00:31:35.554
It's a monster with five eyes, five arms, and five legs.

00:31:35.614 --> 00:31:36.925
Says the tin woodman.

00:31:36.985 --> 00:31:37.585
No.

00:31:37.645 --> 00:31:38.746
Says the lion.

00:31:38.806 --> 00:31:41.815
The wizard is a big ball of fire.

00:31:41.875 --> 00:31:45.537
You're all wrong, says the little man quietly.

00:31:45.597 --> 00:31:49.231
I am the wizard, but I'm not a real wizard.

00:31:49.291 --> 00:31:50.973
I'm from Kansas too.

00:31:50.993 --> 00:31:54.597
I like traveling in hot air balloons.

00:31:54.657 --> 00:31:57.410
That is why I'm here.

00:31:57.470 --> 00:32:01.774
Say the four friends, and they look at each other.

00:32:01.834 --> 00:32:08.015
The people here think I'm a wizard because I come from the sky, says the little man.

00:32:08.075 --> 00:32:11.716
I live inside this palace and never go out.

00:32:11.776 --> 00:32:13.366
No one must see me.

00:32:13.426 --> 00:32:16.087
Everyone must think I'm a real wizard.

00:32:16.147 --> 00:32:21.268
The Scarecrow takes off his glasses and says, The Emerald City isn't green.

00:32:21.328 --> 00:32:26.751
It just looks green because everyone wears green glasses.

00:32:26.811 --> 00:32:28.933
It's a trick.

00:32:28.994 --> 00:32:31.195
Everything here is a trick.

00:32:31.255 --> 00:32:32.955
Yes, it's a trick.

00:32:33.015 --> 00:32:34.766
Says the little man sadly.

00:32:34.826 --> 00:32:40.509
I'm very sorry, but I don't know any magic, so I can't help you.

00:32:40.569 --> 00:32:42.130
You're a bad man.

00:32:42.190 --> 00:32:43.360
Says Dorothy.

00:32:43.420 --> 00:32:48.781
No, I'm a good man, but I am a very bad wizard.

00:32:48.841 --> 00:32:53.583
He says, now the Wicked Witch of the West is dead, says the Scarecrow.

00:32:53.643 --> 00:32:55.503
You must keep your promise.

00:32:55.563 --> 00:32:57.544
I want a brain.

00:32:57.604 --> 00:32:59.434
You're right, says Oz.

00:32:59.494 --> 00:33:01.634
I must keep my promise.

00:33:01.694 --> 00:33:05.635
Come back tomorrow.

00:33:05.696 --> 00:33:10.076
Listening activity.

00:33:10.136 --> 00:33:11.855
One.

00:33:11.915 --> 00:33:14.944
Dear Great Oz, please tell me.

00:33:15.004 --> 00:33:17.376
How can I make a very big head?

00:33:17.436 --> 00:33:21.638
First, you must use lots and lots of paper.

00:33:21.698 --> 00:33:27.022
And with some water, you can make a very big ball.

00:33:27.082 --> 00:33:29.262
Two.

00:33:29.322 --> 00:33:31.464
How do you make the face?

00:33:31.524 --> 00:33:38.838
Well, you paint separate pieces of paper and you put them in the correct places.

00:33:38.898 --> 00:33:41.200
Three.

00:33:41.260 --> 00:33:44.152
How do the eyes and the mouth move?

00:33:44.212 --> 00:33:51.400
Well, you use string or some cord or cotton to pull the eyes and the mouth.

00:33:51.460 --> 00:33:55.554
I sit on the balcony and do this.

00:33:55.614 --> 00:33:57.986
Four.

00:33:58.046 --> 00:34:01.277
What do you do to make the head speak?

00:34:01.337 --> 00:34:07.458
Ah, you see, I am not a wizard, but I am a ventriloquist.

00:34:07.519 --> 00:34:14.702
This means I can speak from one side of the room, but the sound can come from the place where the head is.

00:34:14.722 --> 00:34:22.857
Chapter 7.

00:34:22.917 --> 00:34:32.768
Promises.

00:34:32.828 --> 00:34:41.148
The next morning the four friends go to the wizard's room.

00:34:41.208 --> 00:34:44.429
The scarecrow asks, is my brain ready?

00:34:44.489 --> 00:34:47.279
Please, sit down, says Oz.

00:34:47.340 --> 00:34:49.880
First, I must open your head.

00:34:49.940 --> 00:34:53.211
Then I can put your brain in the right place.

00:34:53.271 --> 00:34:55.182
Now, don't move.

00:34:55.242 --> 00:35:00.223
The little man opens a green box with the word brain on it.

00:35:00.283 --> 00:35:04.300
He slowly puts a brain into the scarecrow's head.

00:35:04.360 --> 00:35:06.438
Now you have a brain.

00:35:06.498 --> 00:35:09.320
You are a very clever scarecrow.

00:35:09.380 --> 00:35:10.350
Says Oz.

00:35:10.410 --> 00:35:11.992
Oh, thank you.

00:35:12.052 --> 00:35:13.392
Says the scarecrow.

00:35:13.452 --> 00:35:15.714
I finally have a brain.

00:35:15.774 --> 00:35:17.785
The Tin Woodman is next.

00:35:17.845 --> 00:35:19.046
He is excited.

00:35:19.106 --> 00:35:20.317
Where is my heart?

00:35:20.377 --> 00:35:21.527
He asks.

00:35:21.588 --> 00:35:27.911
Oz goes to a big green box and takes out a beautiful red heart.

00:35:27.971 --> 00:35:30.968
Here is a special red heart.

00:35:31.029 --> 00:35:34.436
Wear it all the time, says Oz.

00:35:34.496 --> 00:35:36.697
Is it a kind heart?

00:35:36.757 --> 00:35:38.117
Asks the Tin Woodman.

00:35:38.177 --> 00:35:42.299
Yes, it's a very kind heart, says Oz.

00:35:42.359 --> 00:35:43.930
I'm very happy.

00:35:43.990 --> 00:35:46.672
Thank you, says the Tin Woodman.

00:35:46.732 --> 00:35:49.748
Now, I can love someone.

00:35:49.808 --> 00:35:54.355
Now you must give me courage," says the lion.

00:35:54.416 --> 00:35:58.879
Oz gives him a green bottle with the word courage on it.

00:35:58.939 --> 00:36:01.841
Drink this, he says to the lion.

00:36:01.901 --> 00:36:05.649
The lion drinks it quickly and then smiles.

00:36:05.709 --> 00:36:08.206
Now I feel courageous.

00:36:08.266 --> 00:36:10.147
Very courageous.

00:36:10.207 --> 00:36:11.358
Says the lion.

00:36:11.418 --> 00:36:12.830
Thank you.

00:36:12.890 --> 00:36:15.381
And what about Toto and me?

00:36:15.441 --> 00:36:17.453
Ask Dorothy quietly.

00:36:17.513 --> 00:36:20.465
I can take you to Kansas in my hot air balloon.

00:36:20.525 --> 00:36:21.486
Says Oz.

00:36:21.546 --> 00:36:23.167
Come with me.

00:36:23.227 --> 00:36:29.653
They go into his garden and see the big hot air balloon with a small box under it.

00:36:29.713 --> 00:36:35.864
Oz gets into the box and says, come on Dorothy, we're going to Kansas.

00:36:35.924 --> 00:36:41.353
Dorothy says goodbye to the Scarecrow, the Tin Woodman and the Lion.

00:36:41.413 --> 00:36:44.330
Come on, Toto, we're going home to Kansas.

00:36:44.390 --> 00:36:48.013
But Toto suddenly sees a cat and runs after it.

00:36:48.073 --> 00:36:49.774
Toto, come here!

00:36:49.834 --> 00:36:51.005
says Dorothy.

00:36:51.065 --> 00:36:52.686
She runs after Toto.

00:36:52.746 --> 00:36:55.498
Dorothy, the rope is breaking!

00:36:55.558 --> 00:36:56.478
says the wizard.

00:36:56.538 --> 00:36:57.719
Come quickly!

00:36:57.779 --> 00:37:01.572
Dorothy picks up Toto and runs to the hot air balloon.

00:37:01.632 --> 00:37:07.015
But the rope breaks and the big hot air balloon goes up into the sky.

00:37:07.075 --> 00:37:10.198
Go to the land of the quadlings!

00:37:10.258 --> 00:37:11.360
Christ the wizard!

00:37:11.420 --> 00:37:14.743
The good witch of the south lives there!

00:37:14.803 --> 00:37:16.636
She can help you!

00:37:16.696 --> 00:37:18.748
Goodbye!

00:37:18.808 --> 00:37:29.983
The hot air balloon and the wizard disappear into the sky forever.

00:37:30.043 --> 00:37:49.814
Chapter 8 The Good Witch of the South How can I go home now?

00:37:49.874 --> 00:37:51.605
Dorothy asks sadly.

00:37:51.665 --> 00:37:54.087
Where is the land of the Quadlings?

00:37:54.147 --> 00:37:57.378
And who is the Good Witch of the South?

00:37:57.438 --> 00:37:59.788
She starts crying.

00:37:59.848 --> 00:38:03.070
The tin woodman looks at her and starts crying too.

00:38:03.130 --> 00:38:04.402
Don't cry.

00:38:04.462 --> 00:38:05.752
Says the scarecrow.

00:38:05.812 --> 00:38:08.754
Water is bad for your tin body.

00:38:08.814 --> 00:38:11.236
Blow the magic whistle, Dorothy.

00:38:11.296 --> 00:38:12.517
Says the scarecrow.

00:38:12.577 --> 00:38:14.608
The winged monkeys can help you.

00:38:14.668 --> 00:38:16.560
You're a clever scarecrow.

00:38:16.620 --> 00:38:17.861
Says Dorothy.

00:38:17.921 --> 00:38:20.863
She blows the magic whistle.

00:38:20.923 --> 00:38:23.808
And the winged monkeys arrive.

00:38:23.868 --> 00:38:26.553
Please take us to the land of the Quadlings.

00:38:26.613 --> 00:38:30.126
She says, I must find the good witch of the south.

00:38:30.186 --> 00:38:34.930
The winged monkeys take Dorothy and her friends to the land of the Quadlings.

00:38:34.990 --> 00:38:38.103
The land of the Quadlings is lovely.

00:38:38.163 --> 00:38:41.216
There are flowers and trees everywhere.

00:38:41.276 --> 00:38:43.348
All the houses are red.

00:38:43.408 --> 00:38:48.752
The Quadlings are short and they all wear red clothes and red shoes.

00:38:48.812 --> 00:38:52.321
A kind Quadling woman gives them some cake and milk.

00:38:52.381 --> 00:38:54.078
Where is the castle, please?

00:38:54.138 --> 00:38:55.158
Ask Dorothy.

00:38:55.218 --> 00:38:57.349
Take the road to the south.

00:38:57.409 --> 00:38:59.230
Says the kind woman.

00:38:59.290 --> 00:39:06.033
When the friends arrive at the beautiful castle, they see three quaddling girls outside the castle gate.

00:39:06.093 --> 00:39:07.414
Why are you here?

00:39:07.474 --> 00:39:09.674
Asks one girl in a friendly voice.

00:39:09.734 --> 00:39:12.136
I want to see the good witch of the south.

00:39:12.196 --> 00:39:13.236
Says Dorothy.

00:39:13.296 --> 00:39:14.787
Please wait here.

00:39:14.847 --> 00:39:16.368
Says the other girl.

00:39:16.428 --> 00:39:20.189
After a few minutes, the three girls return and say...

00:39:20.249 --> 00:39:21.830
For us, please.

00:39:21.890 --> 00:39:28.046
Soon, Dorothy and her friends enter a big room and see the good witch of the south.

00:39:28.107 --> 00:39:30.620
She is young and beautiful.

00:39:30.680 --> 00:39:33.422
She has red hair and blue eyes.

00:39:33.482 --> 00:39:36.416
She is wearing a long white dress.

00:39:36.476 --> 00:39:39.209
What can I do for you, my child?

00:39:39.269 --> 00:39:40.530
Asks the good witch.

00:39:40.591 --> 00:39:42.606
I want to go home to Kansas.

00:39:42.667 --> 00:39:43.671
says Dorothy.

00:39:43.731 --> 00:39:44.952
Can you help me?

00:39:45.012 --> 00:39:48.706
She looks at Dorothy's silver shoes and smiles.

00:39:48.766 --> 00:39:51.989
Your silver shoes are magic, she says.

00:39:52.049 --> 00:39:54.020
They can take you home.

00:39:54.080 --> 00:40:02.537
First, close your eyes, then click your heels three times and say, take me home to Kansas.

00:40:02.597 --> 00:40:05.336
That's easy, says Dorothy Happily.

00:40:05.396 --> 00:40:06.446
Thank you.

00:40:06.506 --> 00:40:08.357
And what about your friends?

00:40:08.417 --> 00:40:09.518
Says the good witch.

00:40:09.578 --> 00:40:11.138
What do they want?

00:40:11.198 --> 00:40:16.461
I'm a clever scarecrow, and I want to rule the Emerald City.

00:40:16.521 --> 00:40:17.651
Says the scarecrow.

00:40:17.671 --> 00:40:21.163
I have a kind heart, says the Tin Woodman.

00:40:21.223 --> 00:40:27.112
I want to rule the land of the Winkies, because the Wicked Witch of the West is dead.

00:40:27.172 --> 00:40:31.022
I am a courageous lion," says the lion.

00:40:31.082 --> 00:40:34.204
I want to be the king of the forest.

00:40:34.264 --> 00:40:36.465
Good, says the good witch.

00:40:36.525 --> 00:40:39.056
You can all have what you want.

00:40:39.116 --> 00:40:42.158
This is a happy moment for everyone.

00:40:42.218 --> 00:40:47.136
Dorothy kisses the scarecrow, the tin woodman, and the lion.

00:40:47.196 --> 00:40:49.301
Goodbye, my dear friends.

00:40:49.361 --> 00:40:50.242
She says.

00:40:50.302 --> 00:40:51.903
Goodbye, Dorothy.

00:40:51.963 --> 00:40:53.113
And thank you.

00:40:53.173 --> 00:40:58.316
Her friends say, she picks Toto up and closes her eyes.

00:40:58.377 --> 00:41:03.930
Then she clicks her heels three times and says, Take me home to Kansas.

00:41:03.990 --> 00:41:08.122
Suddenly, there is a strong wind.

00:41:08.182 --> 00:41:20.376
It blows her and Toto into the sky and they fly and fly.

00:41:20.437 --> 00:41:28.758
Finally, they are on the ground.

00:41:28.818 --> 00:41:32.698
Dorothy opens her eyes and looks around.

00:41:32.758 --> 00:41:35.379
They are in Kansas.

00:41:35.439 --> 00:41:39.810
She looks at her feet, but her magic shoes aren't there.

00:41:39.870 --> 00:41:43.061
Then she sees Aunt Em and Uncle Henry.

00:41:43.121 --> 00:41:46.371
I'm home again, Aunt Em and Uncle Henry.

00:41:46.431 --> 00:41:48.192
I'm so happy.

00:41:48.252 --> 00:41:59.940
She cries.

00:42:00.000 --> 00:42:12.830
Listening activity.

00:42:12.890 --> 00:42:14.840
One.

00:42:14.900 --> 00:42:17.602
These people are very short.

00:42:17.662 --> 00:42:24.527
They are very friendly, and now they are very happy because the wicked witch of the east is dead.

00:42:24.587 --> 00:42:28.120
They live near the yellow brick road.

00:42:28.180 --> 00:42:30.652
Two.

00:42:30.712 --> 00:42:32.993
This thing is magic.

00:42:33.053 --> 00:42:36.515
When I blow it, it calls the winged monkeys.

00:42:36.575 --> 00:42:40.690
They then do anything you want them to do.

00:42:40.750 --> 00:42:43.804
Three.

00:42:43.864 --> 00:42:47.865
This is one of the wizard's magic tricks.

00:42:47.925 --> 00:42:50.666
It's like a big round paper ball.

00:42:50.726 --> 00:42:53.877
It has eyes, a mouth, and a nose.

00:42:53.937 --> 00:42:56.447
It also talks.

00:42:56.508 --> 00:42:59.088
Four.

00:42:59.148 --> 00:43:02.050
These are very special.

00:43:02.110 --> 00:43:08.142
For your dream to come true, you must click your heels three times and say what you want.

00:43:08.202 --> 00:43:09.202
They're magic.
